## MCP / Harness Hardening Notes

| Issue | Impact | Follow-up |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `safe_new_preview_map` crashed once earlier in the sequence with `TickTaskManager.cpp` assertion during `GEditor->NewMap` | Shared editor map creation can be brittle | Consider deferred NewMap or a safer preview-map reuse path in UnrealMCP |
| Material asset cleanup failed while loaded in Step 1 | Functional PASS but runner cleanup returned FAIL until restart/filesystem delete | Add stronger temp material unload/asset editor close/delete diagnostics |
| Temp characters fall in floorless preview maps | False negative for 3D bounds collection | Character-fixture smokes should freeze movement or create a simple floor |
| Step 6 proves overwrite-to-zero path only | Does not prove persistent Ground hold/decay aesthetics | Keep V4c hold/reproject and visual approval as separate gates |

## Go / No-Go

For the requested smoke list, implementation planning can proceed. The current practical architecture remains:

- Controller collects candidates/components once.
- Select nearest/eligible max 20 active slots per relevant media path.
- Use Array DI 3-chain path for runtime slot data.
- Use component probes for foot/foliage/water source positions, not AnimNotify and not raw bone reads.
- Deactivate non-hold systems only after active slots are zero and RT is confirmed clear.

Remaining work is implementation and visual/performance validation, not a blocker from these smokes.
